      <h2>What I learned</h2>
      <ul class="lp-article-list">
        <li>
          <strong>A successful compile did not tell me much.</strong> The
          first time the app ran in a browser, it hit three bugs. The compiler
          could not catch any of them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>It helped to write my predictions down.</strong> My plan got
          memory right and threading completely wrong. I only know that
          because I wrote the plan down before I started.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>In the browser, a crash in any library is my
          problem.</strong> A Rust panic is a deliberate crash after something
          unexpected happens. When Rust code panics in the browser, the panic
          kills the worker. So I must check a file before I give it to a
          decoder that might panic on it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How I deploy matters as much as the code.</strong> The cache
          kept two files from the same build for different lengths of time.
          That broke every photo for anyone who visited recently.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the browser version is laid out</h2>
      <p>
        The browser version is two programs. The main one runs the window,
        the interface and the graphics on the main thread of the page. A
        second, smaller one runs in Web Workers, which are background threads
        that the browser gives you. It does the slow work of decoding RAW files
        and rendering exports. I needed the second program because a worker
        has no window, so it cannot run the interface or the graphics code.
      </p>

      <figure class="lp-figure">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 214" role="img" aria-label="The browser build. The main thread of the page runs the interface and draws with WebGPU. It reads and writes your folder through the File System Access API. It sends decode and export jobs to a maximum of four Web Workers. Each worker is a separate copy of a smaller WebAssembly program with its own memory. Downloads, compressed: approximately 3.2 MB for the main program and 1.1 MB for the worker.">
